CELL|Hebbian LTP/LTD|NMDA-dependent associative potentiation and depression (Hebb 1949; Bliss & Lomo 1973)|Hebb 1949; Bliss & Lomo 1973 (not re-checked); human support indirect via paired associative stimulation: [Mueller-Dahlhaus 2010](https://publikationen.ub.uni-frankfurt.de/frontdoor/index/index/year/2010/docId/20116)|B|-|S|-|Foundational; local, backprop-free. Direct human synapse-level evidence is limited to LTP-like TMS paradigms.
CELL|Spike-timing-dependent plasticity (STDP)|Order- and interval-dependent sign; human analogue is paired associative stimulation (PAS25/PAS10)|[Mueller-Dahlhaus 2010](https://publikationen.ub.uni-frankfurt.de/frontdoor/index/index/year/2010/docId/20116); [PAS review 2013](https://doi.org/10.3389/fnhum.2013.00823)|C|Y|S|-|PAS is NMDA-dependent and timing-dependent, but mapping to true STDP is debated; protocols differ in mechanism.
CELL|Sliding-threshold metaplasticity (BCM)|Plasticity threshold shifts with postsynaptic activity history|[Homeostatic/metaplastic review (Frontiers 2010)](https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/synaptic-neuroscience/articles/10.3389/fnsyn.2010.00005/pdf); Bienenstock-Cooper-Munro 1982, Abraham & Bear 1996 (not retrieved)|C|-|S|metaplasticity (discrete cascade)|Mostly animal/in vitro. Slow (days). Local.
