CELL|Intrinsic excitability homeostasis|Neuron adjusts own excitability to average activity|[Frontiers 2010 homeostatic review](https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/synaptic-neuroscience/articles/10.3389/fnsyn.2010.00005/pdf)|C|-|S|-|Animal evidence. Analogue of our one-sided KC threshold homeostasis.
CELL|Structural plasticity (spine turnover)|Spine formation then selective elimination; clustered new spines; stabilisation of learning-formed spines|[Clark 2018](https://foil.bme.utexas.edu/publication/clark-2018/clark-2018.pdf); [Hedrick 2022](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1038/s41593-022-01086-6); [Reiner & Dunaevsky 2015](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26098758)|C|Y|S|-|Mouse in-vivo imaging. Whether stabilisation is needed for retention is disputed.
CELL|Synaptic tagging and capture|Weak events tag synapses; plasticity proteins from strong events are captured. Human analogue: behavioural tagging|[Moncada 2015](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4562088/); [STC review](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3240215/)|C|-|S|-|Animal evidence; human behavioural-tagging evidence only as described in the 2015 review. Local; a candidate delayed-credit mechanism.
CELL|Behavioural timescale synaptic plasticity (BTSP)|Plateau-potential-gated potentiation over seconds; one-shot place fields; bidirectional (weak inputs up, strong down)|[Bittner 2017 teaching guide](https://thetransmitter.org/how-to-teach-this-paper/how-to-teach-this-paper-behavioral-time-scale-synaptic-plasticity-underlies-ca1-place-fields-by-bittner-and-milstein-et-al-2017); [Milstein 2021](https://elifesciences.org/articles/73046v2)|C|-|S|-|Mouse CA1 and slices. Local, supports one-shot learning without backprop.
