PERC|Unsupervised sparse feature learning|Receptive fields emerge from natural-image sparsity|Olshausen & Field 1996 (not re-checked)|D|-|M|sparse_geometry|Model reproduces V1 fields; direct causal test limited.
PERC|Cross-modal reorganisation|Deprived cortex recruited by other senses|Sadato 1996 (not re-checked)|B|-|M|-|Human imaging, TMS.
PERC|Attention-gated plasticity|Attended inputs show larger learning|Ahissar & Hochstein; Roelfsema (not re-checked)|B|-|M|-|Human behaviour and imaging.
MOT|Cerebellar supervised learning|Climbing-fibre error instructs Purkinje plasticity (Marr-Albus-Ito)|[Review (PMC4691440)](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4691440); [Gating of neural error signals](https://elifesciences.org/articles/02076)|C|Y|S|-|Teacher is gated; patient evidence general, not mechanistic.
MOT|Two-state motor adaptation|Fast labile plus slow durable processes; savings, interference, spontaneous recovery|[Savings study](https://ir.lib.uwo.ca/brainpub/483); Smith 2006 (named)|B|Y|S|-|Savings account contested (both processes change).
MOT|Implicit vs explicit motor adaptation|Sensory-prediction-error implicit learning vs strategy|[Taylor, Krakauer, Ivry 2014](https://ivrylab.berkeley.edu/files/organized_pubs_pdfs/2014_taylor_krakauer_ivrythe_j.pdf); [McDougle 2015](https://ipalab.princeton.edu/sites/default/files/ipalab/files/mcdougleetal2015.pdf)|B|Y|S|-|Competition between systems vs independence debated.
MOT|Use-dependent plasticity|Repetition biases later movements|Classen 1998 (not re-checked)|B|-|M|-|TMS studies.
MOT|Reward-based motor learning|Exploration guided by reward|Dam 2013 (not re-checked)|B|-|M|-|Human behaviour.
MOT|Motor chunking|Elementary actions bound into chunks vs statistical transitions|[bioRxiv 2021](https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/2021.02.12.430894v1.full); [conscious intent study](https://learnmem.cshlp.org/content/21/9/449.short)|B|Y|S|-|Diedrichsen & Kornysheva 2015 named, not retrieved.
MOT|Forward models and efference copy|Predict sensory consequences of actions|Wolpert 1995 (not re-checked)|B|-|M|-|Behaviour, patients.
LANG|Critical period for language|Grammar learning ability steady to about 17.4 years then declines|[Hartshorne 2018](https://dspace.mit.edu/handle/1721.1/126641)|B|Y|S|-|Large dataset with computational model; emergentist reading proposed later.
LANG|Natural pedagogy / ostensive cues|Infants expect communicated information to generalise|[Natural pedagogy evidence summary](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/29315501)|C|Y|S|-|Gaze-following replications challenged a central pillar; no comprehensive meta-analysis found.
LANG|Over-imitation|Children copy causally unnecessary actions|[Lyons 2007](https://cogdevlab.yale.edu/sites/default/files/files/overimitation%202007.pdf); [Whiten review](https://research-repository.st-andrews.ac.uk/bitstream/10023/21213/1/Whiten_OverImitation_DevRev_AAM.pdf)|B|Y|S|-|Robust phenomenon; causal-encoding vs normative accounts debated.
LANG|Mirror system / action observation|Motor regions respond to observed actions; role in understanding contested|[Heyes & Catmur 2021](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8785302)|C|Y|S|-|Contributes to low-level processing; high-level interpretation not supported.
LANG|Observational learning|Learning by watching models|Bandura 1977 (not re-checked)|A|-|M|-|Robust behaviour.
LANG|Cumulative culture|Teaching and imitation allow ratcheting|Tomasello 1999; Henrich (not re-checked)|B|Y|M|-|Cross-cultural evidence; mechanism debated.
LANG|Synaptic overproduction and pruning|Synapse density peaks in early childhood, then declines; pruning may last into third decade|[Huttenlocher/Petanjek (PMC3156171)](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3156171)|B|Y|S|-|Postmortem human data; timing disputed.
LANG|Phonetic perceptual narrowing / sensitive periods|Infant discrimination narrows to native categories|Werker; Kuhl (not re-checked)|B|-|M|-|Behavioural.
LANG|Vocal learning and babbling|Sensorimotor loop between production and hearing|Not searched|B|-|M|-|Developmental behaviour.
LANG|Play and exploratory learning|Self-directed exploration|Gopnik et al. (not re-checked)|C|Y|M|-|Evidence of causal benefit limited.
LANG|Scaffolding / zone of proximal development|Guided learning just beyond independent level|Vygotsky 1978; Wood 1976 (not re-checked)|C|Y|M|-|Behavioural classroom evidence.
LANG|Starting small / staged curricula|Limited early capacity may aid learning (Elman)|Elman 1993 (not re-checked)|D|Y|M|-|Model result; human evidence mixed.
NUM|Neuronal recycling of the number sense|Symbolic arithmetic reuses parietal numerosity and language circuits|[Dehaene & Cohen 2007](https://www.Gwern.net/doc/culture/2007-cohen.pdf)|B|Y|S|-|Imaging dissociations (subtraction parietal; multiplication language-related).
NUM|Approximate number system training|Approximate-arithmetic practice transfers to symbolic arithmetic|[Editorial on ANS and mathematics](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6751380/); [Frontiers 2018](https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/integrative-neuroscience/articles/10.3389/fnint.2018.00028/pdf)|C|Y|S|-|Original and one replication positive; a systematic review finds no conclusive evidence.
NUM|Number-line linearisation and board games|Linear games build magnitude mapping|[Laski & Siegler 2013](https://www.cmu.edu/dietrich/psychology/cs/research-teaching/docs/2013LaskiSieglerNumberBoardGames.pdf)|B|-|S|-|Mostly one research group; replication worth checking.
NUM|Counting-to-retrieval shift|Counting gives way to memory retrieval with hippocampal growth|[Qin 2014](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4286364)|B|-|S|-|Longitudinal fMRI in 7-9-year-olds.
NUM|Overlapping waves / strategy choice|Counting-all, min, decomposition and retrieval coexist and shift|[Frankfurt study (secondary)](https://publikationen.ub.uni-frankfurt.de/opus4/files/31705/26478-88720-1-SM.pdf)|B|-|S|-|Siegler primary sources not retrieved.
NUM|Fact-retrieval interference network|Retrieval competes among stored facts; problem-size effect from confusability|[Campbell-style interference review](https://link.springer.com/article/10.3758/s13423-020-01818-4)|B|Y|S|-|Cross-operation errors robust; model called unfalsifiable by critics and does not fit all data.
NUM|Conceptual-procedural iteration|Concepts and procedures improve each other in alternation|[Rittle-Johnson 2001](https://alibali.psych.wisc.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/371/2018/02/Rittle-JohnsonSieglerAlibali2001.pdf)|B|Y|S|-|Direction of influence debated for fractions.
NUM|Finger counting and finger training|Finger-based calculation supports early addition|[French kindergarten training](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11693818/); [longitudinal study](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8869778/)|C|Y|S|-|Positive training results conflict with a German null vs active control.
NUM|Working memory in multi-digit carries|Phonological, visuospatial and executive resources store interim results and carries|[NTU study](https://irep.ntu.ac.uk/id/eprint/41019); [Vallee-Tourangeau 2016](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5256453/)|B|Y|S|-|Format (columnar vs linear) changes the resource used.
NUM|Instance-based automatisation / power law of practice|Practice speeds retrieval of stored instances|[Logan 1988](https://pcl.sitehost.iu.edu/rgoldsto/courses/cogscilearning/loganautomaticity.pdf); [Rickard 1997](https://rickardlab.ucsd.edu/pdf/Rickard1997.pdf)|B|Y|S|-|Power law fits within strategies but not across strategy shifts.
NUM|Single-neuron number codes|Human MTL neurons tuned to number and rules|Kutter 2018, 2022 (cited earlier in project notes; not re-checked)|B|-|M|-|Human single-unit recordings.
NUM|Spatial-numerical association (mental number line)|Number magnitude mapped to space|Dehaene 1993 (not re-checked)|B|Y|M|-|Replicable behaviour; interpretation debated.
EDU|Retrieval practice (testing effect)|Testing beats restudy; feedback adds|[Frontiers 2018 analysis citing both meta-analyses](https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fpsyg.2018.02412/pdf)|A|-|S|-|Rowland 2014 g~0.50 (feedback ~0.73 vs ~0.39 without); Adesope 2017 g~0.61 (secondary figures).
EDU|Spacing effect|Distributed practice beats massed; optimal gap rises with retention interval|[Cepeda 2006](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16719566/)|A|-|S|-|839 assessments, 317 experiments.
EDU|Expanding / lag schedules|Longer lags and expanding intervals|[Cepeda 2006](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16719566/)|B|Y|S|-|Benefit depends on retention interval.
EDU|Interleaving|Mixed practice improves category/problem discrimination|[Brunmair & Richter 2019](https://www.psychologie.uni-wuerzburg.de/fileadmin/06020400/2019/Brunmair_Richter_in_press__2019_META-ANALYSIS_OF_INTERLEAVED_LEARNING.pdf)|A|-|S|-|59 studies, g=0.42; larger for visual material; small for mathematics.
EDU|Worked examples / expertise reversal|Studying solutions helps novices; benefit disappears for experts|[Frontiers 2022](https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/psychology/articles/10.3389/fpsyg.2022.1032003/pdf); Barbieri et al. 2023 meta-analysis (named in results; findings not retrieved)|B|Y|S|-|Many reversal studies use subjective load measures.
EDU|Generation effect|Self-generated items are remembered better|[Bertsch 2007](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17645161/)|A|-|S|-|86 studies/445 effect sizes, d=0.40; effort account weakened.
EDU|Informative feedback|Feedback content determines learning gain|[Wisniewski 2020](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6987456/)|A|-|S|-|435 studies, d=0.48; heterogeneous; timing findings not retrieved.
EDU|Self-explanation|Prompted self-explanation improves learning|[Bisra 2018](https://www.Gwern.net/doc/psychology/spaced-repetition/2018-bisra.pdf)|A|-|S|-|69 effect sizes, g=0.55.
EDU|Productive failure|Problem solving before instruction aids transfer|[Coverage of Sinha & Kapur 2021](https://www.weforum.org/stories/2021/09/students-who-productively-fail-learn-more/)|B|Y|S|-|53 studies/166 comparisons per press summaries; depends on design fidelity and prior knowledge.
EDU|Hypercorrection|High-confidence errors corrected more often|[Butterfield & Metcalfe line](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3079415)|B|-|S|-|Replicated in many single-lab studies; no multi-lab replication found.
EDU|Desirable difficulties|Slower acquisition conditions improve retention|Bjork 1994 (not re-checked)|B|Y|M|-|Umbrella for several effects above.
EDU|Levels of processing / elaboration|Deeper semantic encoding improves retention|[Craik & Tulving 1975 summary](https://www.simplypsychology.org/levelsofprocessing.html); [2024 forgetting-rate study](https://link.springer.com/article/10.3758/s13421-024-01599-4)|B|Y|S|-|Circularity criticism; transfer-appropriate processing can outweigh depth.
EDU|Mnemonics / method of loci|Spatial imagery scaffold for list memory|[Dresler 2017 coverage](https://med.stanford.edu/news/all-news/2017/03/memorization-tool-bulks-up-brains-internal-connections.html)|B|-|S|-|Six-week training raised recall and moved connectivity toward memory athletes; small samples.
EDU|Expert chunking and templates|Experts store large pattern libraries; long-term templates|[Gobet & Simon 1996](https://www.Gwern.net/doc/psychology/chess/1996-gobet.pdf)|B|-|S|-|Chess-heavy evidence; about 50,000 chunks estimated for masters.
EDU|Dual coding|Verbal plus visual codes|Paivio 1971 (not re-checked)|B|-|M|-|Behavioural.
EDU|Transfer-appropriate processing|Retention best when study and test processes match|Morris, Bransford, Franks 1977 (not re-checked)|B|-|M|-|Behavioural.
EDU|Metacognitive monitoring and control|Judgements of learning guide study allocation|Nelson & Narens 1990 (not re-checked)|B|Y|M|-|Calibration often poor.
EDU|Cognitive load theory|Instructional design limited by working memory|Sweller 1988 (not re-checked)|B|Y|M|-|Subjective load measures; some claims untested.
EDU|Deliberate practice|Effortful targeted practice builds expertise|Ericsson 1993 (not re-checked)|B|Y|M|-|Effect size of practice debated.
MOD|Cholinergic encoding mode|High ACh favours encoding; low favours retrieval/reactivation|[Gedankien 2025 reviewed preprint](https://elifesciences.org/reviewed-preprints/108972)|B|-|S|-|Human intracranial scopolamine: encoding impairment, not retrieval.
MOD|Noradrenergic arousal and plasticity|LC-noradrenaline boosts salient memories|[Human 7T study](https://elifesciences.org/articles/52059); [propranolol study](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC263864)|A|-|S|-|Also impairs memory for neutral items before arousing events in some models.
MOD|Stress hormones and consolidation|Cortisol alters consolidation and retrieval|Roozendaal 2002; Wolf 2009 (not re-checked)|B|Y|M|-|Dose and timing dependent.
MOD|Serotonin and aversive learning|Opponent role to dopamine; behavioural inhibition|Daw 2002; Dayan & Huys (not re-checked)|C|Y|M|-|Mostly animal and model.
